  <!--Q7-->
  <exercise data-content-id="0c572bab-4c76-49cd-b643-d03e1d90bfd4" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="-0.87" data-solution-options="[&quot;-0.32&quot;, &quot;0.87&quot;, &quot;-0.87&quot;, &quot;0.32&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>7. Which of the following correlation coefficients would best describe this scatter plot?</para>
      <para><figure><media alt="SCATTER PLOT THAT SHOWS THE RELATIONSHIP BETWEEN AGE IN YEARS AND PRICE IN DOLLARS. THE SCATTER PLOT SHOWS A VERY STRONG NEGATIVE CORRELATION."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/a3e5f256443b7065f434b4f2805fb6d9fdcf58d1"/></media></figure></para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(-0.87\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 3.4.2 – 3.4.5.
      </para>
    </div>
