      </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Q9-->
  <exercise data-content-id="f1067638-02fd-4a21-a383-8692cafdae54" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="1" data-solution="Scatter plot B" data-solution-options="[&quot;Scatter plot A&quot;, &quot;Scatter plot B&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>9. Which of the following has the stronger linear relationship? Explain.</para>
      <para>Scatter Plot A:</para>
      <para><figure><media alt="SCATTER PLOT THAT SHOWS A MODERATE POSITIVE CORRELATION."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/81ba1809d00f11bd8a2eed30d83f45a385d8823d"/></media></figure></para>
      <para>Scatter Plot B:</para>
      <para><figure><media alt="SCATTER PLOT THAT SHOWS A STRONG POSITIVE CORRELATION."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/0e8567567754afd2ed200992508ac9e43957b2a0"/></media></figure></para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! Scatter plot B because the points in the scatter plot are closer to forming a linear relationship. </para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 3.4.2.
      </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Q10-->
  <exercise data-content-id="a9404ec6-8710-4e20-9345-d00023ddc075" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="0.43" data-solution-options="[&quot;-0.89&quot;, &quot;0.89&quot;, &quot;0.43&quot;, &quot;-0.43&quot;]">
